window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-8efdbfd54bb46e81"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"calibrate-assessments\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">校准评估评分</h1> <p>在不打分或更改成绩的情况下，检查评分模式。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT，根据去标识化后的作业提交、评分量规、评分导出数据和示例反馈，制作一份校准工作簿，其中包含证据标记、评分模式检查和量规澄清建议。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要在不同班级或评阅者之间校准评分的教师。</li> <li>需要为每项标记提供证据的去标识化评估审核。</li> <li>需要进一步明确标准或示例的评分量规。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>在便于审核的工作簿中比较量规标准、评分模式和证据。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>汇总反馈主题，并起草澄清量规的建议。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>创建评分校准工作簿</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请审核我提供的去标识化作业提交、评分量规、评分导出数据、示例反馈、课程学习成果和校准规则。\n\n请创建一份校准工作簿，用于：\n- 标出可能存在的评分不一致\n- 汇总常见优点和不足\n- 归纳反馈主题\n- 提出澄清评分量规的建议\n- 为每项标记引用证据\n\n不要评分或更改成绩。所有评分判断都应交由教师审核。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"de-identify-and-define-the-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">先去标识化并明确审核范围</h2> <p>在分享作业提交或评分导出数据之前，移除直接身份标识信息。提供评分量规、课程学习成果、校准规则和有代表性的反馈，以便 ChatGPT 按预期标准比较证据。</p> <p>说明审核可以标记哪些问题，以及哪些事项必须由教师决定。</p> <p><a id=\"create-the-calibration-workbook\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">创建评分校准工作簿</h2> <p>使用起始提示词生成一份工作簿，分别列出：</p> <ul> <li>评分量规标准和预期证据</li> <li>分数分布和可能的不一致</li> <li>有代表性的示例</li> <li>常见优点和学习缺口</li> <li>反馈主题</li> <li>需要共同审核的案例</li> </ul> <p>把每项标记都当作供审核的线索，而不是评分决定。</p> <p><a id=\"validate-the-findings\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">验证分析结果</h2> <p>教师审核者应检查源证据、确认比较对象具有可比性，并查找可能缺失的背景信息，例如便利安排或作业变体。不要使用该工作簿来评分、改分或自动确定最终成绩。</p> <p>审核完成后，请 ChatGPT 将已确认的模式整理成拟议的量规澄清内容和校准示例。对于尚不确定的案例，应明确保留未决状态。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"calibrate-assessments\">Calibrate assessments</h1> <p>Review scoring patterns without assigning or changing grades.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with de-identified submissions, rubrics, grading exports, and sample feedback to create a calibration workbook with evidence flags, scoring-pattern checks, and rubric clarification recommendations.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Faculty calibrating grading across sections or reviewers.</li> <li>De-identified assessment reviews that need evidence for every flag.</li> <li>Rubrics that may need clearer criteria or examples.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Compare rubric criteria, score patterns, and evidence in a reviewable workbook.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Synthesize feedback themes and draft rubric clarification recommendations.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create an Assessment Calibration Workbook</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the de-identified submissions, rubric, grading export, sample feedback, course outcomes, and calibration rules I provide.\n\nCreate a calibration workbook that:\n- flags possible scoring inconsistencies\n- summarizes common strengths and gaps\n- identifies feedback themes\n- suggests rubric clarifications\n- cites evidence for every flag\n\nDo not assign or change grades. Route every scoring judgment to faculty review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"de-identify-and-define-the-review\">De-identify and define the review</h2> <p>Remove direct identifiers before sharing submissions or grading exports. Provide the rubric, course outcomes, calibration rules, and representative feedback so ChatGPT can compare evidence against the intended criteria.</p> <p>State what the review may flag and what must remain a faculty decision.</p> <h2 id=\"create-the-calibration-workbook\">Create the calibration workbook</h2> <p>Use the starter prompt to produce a workbook that separates:</p> <ul> <li>rubric criteria and expected evidence</li> <li>score distributions and possible inconsistencies</li> <li>representative examples</li> <li>common strengths and learning gaps</li> <li>feedback themes</li> <li>cases that need joint review</li> </ul> <p>Treat every flag as a review lead, not a grading decision.</p> <h2 id=\"validate-the-findings\">Validate the findings</h2> <p>Faculty reviewers should check the source evidence, confirm that comparisons are like-for-like, and look for missing context such as accommodations or assignment variants. Do not use the workbook to assign, alter, or automate final grades.</p> <p>After review, ask ChatGPT to turn confirmed patterns into proposed rubric clarifications and calibration examples. Keep uncertain cases visibly unresolved.</p>"};
